  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/c0110eee-03de-4d76-8cfe-c230ca2b6d0c.png\" style=\"width:2.72708in;height:1.51319in\" /><br />One of the normal from <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />hence, assume <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br />and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Then, the slope of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br />The equation of the normal at <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br />Putting&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in the above equation, we get,<br /><math><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>56</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>.</mo></math>",
